From: Spaceghost <spaceghost@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] examples: keep standalone export stubs with Clang

The function body emits globally visible assembly entry points. Clang can
otherwise discard the function and its inline assembly because the function
itself has no C callers. Mark it used so Zig's Clang frontend retains the
export stubs without falling back to GCC.

---
 examples/standalone/stubs.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/examples/standalone/stubs.c b/examples/standalone/stubs.c
index 3e6f9af..fc15915 100644
--- a/examples/standalone/stubs.c
+++ b/examples/standalone/stubs.c
@@ -273,6 +273,6 @@ gd_t *global_data;
 static
 #endif /* GCC_VERSION */
-void __attribute__((unused)) dummy(void)
+void __attribute__((used)) dummy(void)
 {
 #include <_exports.h>
 }
-- 
2.30.2
